\begin{dfn} \label{dfn:225}
Let $\a$ be a finitely generated ideal in $A$, and let $M$ be an $A$-module. We 
say that $M$ is {\em $\a$-adically flat} if $\opn{Tor}^{A}_q(N, M) = 0$
for every $\a$-torsion $A$-module $N$ and every $q > 0$. 
\end{dfn}

This definition is copied from \cite{Ye2}. In \cite{BS2}, \cite{CS} 
the term used is {\em $\a$-completely flat}.
Here is a useful characterization of this property. 

